WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.740
Those aren't depth charges, are they?

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.040
What is that sound?

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.870
That's...

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.710
As I've guessed.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.710
They not only heard us blow our ballast tanks at 90 meters down,

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.090
they also know exactly where we are.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.920
Looks like your ship is really as good as they say.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.300
Such amazing ears it has...

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.430
I won't let you do this!!

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.350
Yanagi! Morse Code!

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.980
Tell the Mirai to get out of here!!

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.310
B-B-But how?!

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.940
Grab something and hit the walls!

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.320
Y-Yes! H-Hey! What are you doing?

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.900
An excellent ship and a brave commander.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.490
However, that will be the downfall of the Mirai...

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.740
- Let go!
- Let us go!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.870
What do you think you're doing?! What do you plan to do with us?!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.910
Hold on! Explain yourself!

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.210
C-Commander!!

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:36.960
T-They've stopped?

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.800
The sub has stopped surfacing!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.300
Current depth is 5 meters!

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.110
Here... they come!!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:58.110
One Versus Forty

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.040
About 40 targets spotted at 80 degrees, distance 15 miles.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.470
Target sighted 30 degrees right!

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.090
It's a cruiser class.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.220
I'm sure of it.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.180
It's them.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.360
You never change, do you, Lieutenant Jones?

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.200
So be it, you take the lead.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.530
Target in sight!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.660
But don't let your guard down, Jones.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.870
We still don't know what kind of weapons this ship has.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.460
All planes! Attack formation!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:57.040
Roger! Forming attack formation now!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.340
Descending to 200 meters!

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.280
Masayuki, its up to you now.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.120
Yosuke and myself...

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.290
We have killed with our hands to protect the Mirai.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.620
Masayuki, the fate of...

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.420
...the Mirai's 240 crew...

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.380
...lies in your hands now.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.780
Torpedo planes! Follow behind Jones!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.870
Go up to 3000!

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.050
That's Lieutenant Hutton for you.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.800
Even without a radio,

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.970
he's still able to lead his squadron perfectly.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.640
I wonder what on earth he would be doing...

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.520
...without this darn war on.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.230
Let's just enjoy the view from up here. That poor cruiser.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.610
I hate to say it, but she's already as good as sunk.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.660
80 degrees, range 7 miles.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.990
All missile units, prepare to fire!

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.710
Target group alpha! 13 planes!

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.000
80 degrees!

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.670
Distance! 5 miles and closing!!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.670
Target group, Bravo! 22 planes!

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.500
170 degrees, 6 miles!

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:09.340
This ship's Aegis system is capable of...

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.800
...tracking 128 targets at a time.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.640
If the auto-fire mode is used,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.230
all 40 planes, or 80 lives,

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.020
will be destroyed at the push of a button.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.610
Missile units! Load missiles into launchers!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.490
Prepare for an immediate launch on my command!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.820
Load missiles!

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.530
He's firing manually? And only 6 missiles?!

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.540
Well, it is Lieutenant Kikuchi...

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.040
Wait! I know what he is doing!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.840
With a focused attack on one small group,

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.920
the morale of the other pilots will be crushed.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.260
By doing this, we can save our ammo and drive them away!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.050
Impressive!

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.390
He's shaking?!

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:58.810
The Lieutenant is normally as cool as a cucumber,

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.810
he never even broke a sweat in all the simulations we did.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.000
Mirai. 30 degrees to starboard.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.880
So, Lieutenant Taki.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.470
What do we do next?

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.300
We've got front row seats here,

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.800
just sit back and enjoy the show.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.760
Surface next to the Mirai.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.230
I made the wrong decision.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.020
Now the Mirai's in the middle of...

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.230
...a battle that she could have avoided.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.070
Don't worry so much.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.450
With a top speed of 40 knots, the Mirai was designed to...

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.070
...handle not only sea battles, but also establish complete...

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.080
...air superiority with its missile defenses.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.250
She'll take out those planes in no time flat.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.910
It doesn't matter what planes...

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.250
...they send, because nothing in this time has a chance.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.260
Regardless of the age, machines don't fight wars!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.930
Battles are...

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.640
...fought by men.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.440
All planes ready for attack!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.570
5 miles to target!

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:40.620
What can she do with just one deck gun?!

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.500
All units stand by!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.170
Ready deck gun, open fire!

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.460
Track Number, 6688.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.500
Deck gun, start firing!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.470
Start firing!

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.690
From Track Number 6688,

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.650
6630 taken down!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.070
New target! 210 degrees!

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.000
Lieutenant! The Torpedo Planes!!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:42.010
Jones?! N-No, wait!

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.390
Track Number 6644, coming in hard!

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.560
Firing Sea Sparrows!! Salvo!!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.920
Jones!!

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.170
Jones!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.880
W-What's happening?!

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.760
Report! Any damage?!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.430
We're okay, Lieutenant! The wing and the fuselage...

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.100
...just picked up a few dings!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.100
Alright!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.610
Watch out!!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.930
It was like a flying torpedo that came right at us.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.760
It self-destructed just 100 yards before nailing us.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.680
The sender of the warning message called it...

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.140
...the "Arrow of Sagittarius".

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:12.980
An arrow from god that always hits its target.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.540
It only looks like it isn't well-armed.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.080
That filthy rat!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.580
Normal attacks won't sink this ship.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.670
Ensign! You've saved my life many times in battle, right?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.010
- Yes?
- Get out now!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.010
Huh? B-But why?!

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.970
Look in front!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.560
We're leaking oil.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.270
This plane's going down.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:58.650
Unfortunately, I don't think we'll make it back to the Wasp.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.030
That ship seems to have stopped its attacks.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.610
Watch out for shrapnel on your way down!

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:07.200
What about you, Lieutenant?! Don't tell me?!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.700
Don't worry.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.500
I don't plan on dying here.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.920
However, I'm sure that this ship's still hiding something.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.130
I'm going to find out what it is.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.510
I'm going to complete the mission, no matter what.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.730
Lieutenant Taki! Something incredible...

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.020
That ship shot down over 10 planes in the blink of an eye.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.650
What exactly is that ship?!

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.930
Masayuki,

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.640
please forgive me.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.390
Mirai, please survive.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.740
Target group Bravo.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.820
Verified 14 planes down.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.740
Target group Echo. 6 planes down.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.910
Target group, Bravo! Target detected!

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.700
45 degrees, 3 planes!!

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.000
330 degrees, 2 planes!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.380
170 degrees, 3 planes approaching!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.090
In the span of one minute,

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.880
they've lost more than half of their planes.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:50.350
They now are left with less than half their force intact.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.100
Why don't they retreat?!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.020
Track Number 6656!

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.980
Approaching fast!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.980
CIC Deck! Plane sighted! Starboard 60 degrees!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.070
It's coming right at us!

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.490
Lieutenant! I'm leaving first!!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.490
Okay! See you later!!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.090
It's too late for the Sea Sparrow.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.760
Listen up! Activate the Phalanx system!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.310
Distance, 1500.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:38.190
Okay! Target locked!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:41.190
Let's see how you like my thousand pound bomb!

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.420
Our defense wasn't perfect.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:09.170
The fear of taking out 80 lives at one go,

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.800
made me pull my punches...

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:14.180
...and not use all the weapons I could have.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.930
I still wasn't really ready...

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.980
...for a real battle...

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:38.000
All units!! Check for damage immediately!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.580
Breakdown on deck number 2!

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.600
Target spotted!! Coming in steep!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.560
What?!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.650
Angle of attack, 80 degrees.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.200
I've never come in this steep before.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.910
I must be... going crazy!

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.870
You filthy creep!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.580
Come on and show me what you've got!!

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.710
He's still not pulling up?!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.130
Hard to starboard now!!

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.590
All crew! Get starboard!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.220
All crew! Brace for impact!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.350
Hard to starboard! All crew!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.520
Get starboard! All crew! Brace for impact!

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.770
- Hard to starboard!
- If we're defeated here,

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.150
we'll never make it home!

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:55.820
A Dauntless hitting the Mirai! It's a collision of the century!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.280
I'm not going to miss this one!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.420
I can't believe that pilot is so reckless!

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.680
Emotions of fear and anger...

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.430
...cloud judgment.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.430
Even if one survives, if he doesn't destroy his opponent...

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:26.480
He will be destroyed by his opponent.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.940
However, we've failed to realize this basic truth...

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.690
It's going to hit us!!

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.900
...until now when it's far too late!

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.210
- Chief?!
- You fool!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.170
Don't get scared over one little American plane!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.090
Stop being such a coward and get up!!

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.100
Hurry up!

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.060
Sir!

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.190
Darn it! That Yosuke creep!

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.480
Is he watching the whole show from the safety of the submarine?

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.410
Takasugi! Asada! Are you alright?!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:28.420
The airplane has hit the deck!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.840
The 120 mm gun has been damaged!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.960
Extent of other damage not yet known!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:39.470
We are still checking the extent of the damage!

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.600
Emergency Units! Go put out the fire now!

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:45.640
Ready medical teams to treat the wounded!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:45.720
Navigation Officer

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.140
Signal officer!

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.520
I'm okay.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.860
But...

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.040
The helm and communications systems...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.920
...are still functioning.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.040
This ship is still alright!

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:16.090
Hurry up and put the fire out!!

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.470
Lieutenant!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.980
The radar interference disappeared from the scopes!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.650
This is Squadron 6 calling the Wasp!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.320
We hit the ship once, but it wasn't enough to sink it!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:24.700
We lost two thirds of our planes to its anti-air defenses.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:28.660
It has weapons that we haven't seen before.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.290
Two thirds of the squadron!?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.330
Request permission to launch second attack!

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.000
Hutton's been defeated?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.210
A second attack please!!

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.680
This is the Wasp calling Squadron 6!

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.350
All planes to return now!

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.230
I repeat! We are preparing for a second attack!

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.240
This is the Wasp!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.650
All Squadron 6 planes are to return now!

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:09.780
We are now preparing for a second attack!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.040
These guys don't know when to quit!

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:25.550
Do you think we can keep fighting them?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.940
On the battlefield, resolve is most important.

00:21:57.290 --> 00:22:00.590
Captain, I suggest that we use...

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:03.130
...a Tomahawk missile to sink the Wasp.

00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:17.330
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:22.570
Just peacefully

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:34.380
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:47.260
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:53.870
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:59.940
I kept on praying

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:11.790
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:27.470
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:42.390
Even if it's for self-defense,

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:45.180
it still doesn't give you the excuse to kill this many people!

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:47.100
Masayuki! Do you understand?!

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:50.230
One push of the button would destroy more than 1000 lives!

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:53.400
The Allied Forces see us as the enemy.

00:23:53.770 --> 00:23:55.440
If we don't acknowledge this fact,

00:23:55.440 --> 00:23:57.110
we won't even be able to protect ourselves!

00:23:57.110 --> 00:23:59.320
That isn't what we wished for!

00:23:59.610 --> 00:24:01.910
The power of Mirai isn't for claiming lives!

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:04.950
Next Episode: Warning

00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:04.370
Tomahawk, one minute to impact!

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
